  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Adds a public CPython-compatible int64 annotation and checked conversion, fully typed signed-word locals/calls/returns/comparisons/ranges, overflow-safe arithmetic with Python floor division and remainder, direct typed Int64Buffer access, and native/word/tagged/fmpz/JavaScript/Wasm lowering. Existing unannotated Int64Buffer reads retain exact-Integer semantics; an int64 expected context selects the allocation-free path.",
    "risks": [
      "Only Linux x64 has been exercised locally; the portable overflow helpers and LLP64 conversion paths still require normal Windows, macOS, and Linux arm64 CI.",
      "Signed shifts and exponentiation are intentionally outside this first scalar surface.",
      "The optimizer opportunity manifest becomes stale whenever compiler inputs change and must be regenerated by the integration lane; this lane does not claim generated dashboard artifacts.",
      "The native-integration package is at 1049999 of its 1050000-byte allowance, so follow-up compiler growth should first recover source weight rather than increase the allowance."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate after agent/mixed-exact-float-sidecar, then regenerate and review the optimizer opportunity dashboard artifacts.",
      "Run the frozen splitting-degree catalog with explicit int64 locals and Int64Buffer storage to measure promotion-free generated C and kernel time.",
      "Let platform CI exercise the signed conversion and overflow paths on Windows x64, macOS arm64, and Linux arm64."
    ]
